So, 

\[375 \times 775 = 375 \times (700 + 75) = (375 \times 700) + (375 \times 75).\]

Now, we will calculate each term separately.

First, calculate \(375 \times 700\):

\[375 \times 700 = (375 \times 7) \times 100.\]

Now, calculate \(375 \times 7\):

\[375 \times 7 = 2625.\]

Then multiply the result by 100:

\[2625 \times 100 = 262500.\]

So, 

\[375 \times 700 = 262500.\]

Next, we calculate \(375 \times 75\).

To simplify \(375 \times 75\), we can use the distributive property again and express 75 as \(75 = 70 + 5\). Therefore,

\[375 \times 75 = 375 \times (70 + 5) = (375 \times 70) + (375 \times 5).\]

Now, we calculate each term separately.

First, calculate \(375 \times 70\):

\[375 \times 70 = (375 \times 7) \times 10.\]

