\[375 \times 70 = 2625 \times 10 = 26250.\]

Next, calculate \(375 \times 5\):

\[375 \times 5 = 1875.\]

Now, add the two results together:

\[375 \times 75 = 26250 + 1875 = 28125.\]

So, 

\[375 \times 75 = 28125.\]

Now we have the two parts from our original distribution:

\[375 \times 775 = (375 \times 700) + (375 \times 75) = 262500 + 28125.\]

Finally, add these two results together:

\[262500 + 28125 = 290625.\]

Therefore, the product of 375 and 775 is \(\boxed{290625}.\)
